== Quests & Progression

=== Quest Types

- *Village quests* — single-player, set in Kamura. They tell the story and teach the game; their star rating climbs as you complete them.
- *Hub quests* — posted at the Gathering Hub, scaled for multiplayer (solo works too, it just takes longer). Hub quests are where *Hunter Rank (HR)* lives: they unlock the real progression.
- *Urgent quests* — quests marked as urgent that gate the next star tier. Clear the urgent to advance.
- *Event quests* — special quests with unique rewards; download/install from the game's event quest list when available.
- *Subquests* — optional checklists (hunt X, gather Y) running alongside your main quest. They pay extra rewards; pick ones matching what you will do anyway.

#tip[
  Subquests are free rewards. Glance at the checklist before posting a quest and you will finish most of them by accident.
]

=== Low Rank → High Rank

- The village story takes you through *Low Rank* (LR) — the tutorial that doubles as a campaign.
- The *Rampage* is High Rank's signature trial: a siege defense of Kamura where you man weapons and walls against waves of monsters. It gates your HR progress — embrace it as a change of pace, not a chore.
- Hub quests climb into *High Rank (HR)*: harder monsters, better materials, and the gear that matters. Hub HR is where base-game Monster Hunter actually starts.

=== Into Sunbreak (Master Rank)

The *Sunbreak* expansion adds a third tier on top: *Master Rank (MR)*, based in Elgado, with harder monsters and MR-only equipment. Wave 0's job ends at the door to MR — the expedition is Wave 1's story (see Part 4). What you learn here — the loop, your weapon, your habits — is exactly what MR will test.

=== Multiplayer Basics

- Post a quest with *Join Request* enabled and other hunters can drop in; you can also join others' requests.
- Play politely: wait for everyone at the start, don't steal the host's kills/captures, and let the host decide capture-vs-kill. (Part 5 has the full etiquette.)
- Monster health scales with party size, so hunting with four is faster than soloing — but solo practice is where skill is built.

=== Progression Summary

*Village story (LR) → Hub HR + Rampage → [Sunbreak] Master Rank → Anomaly Investigations (Part 5).*

The game will keep handing you the next step; follow the markers, do the urgents, and upgrade gear when a wall appears. If you hit a wall, the answer is almost never "grind more" — it is *armor upgrades, the right element, and learning the pattern*.
